<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 08_typography/10: Text transform -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Text transform</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .tt p { font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0.4rem 0; }
    .up { text-transform: uppercase; } .low { text-transform: lowercase; } .cap { text-transform: capitalize; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Text transform</h1>
    <p class="lead">Changing case with CSS, not by retyping.</p>
    <div class="tt">
      <p class="up">uppercase: The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog</p>
      <p class="low">LOWERCASE: THE QUICK BROWN FOX JUMPS OVER THE LAZY DOG</p>
      <p class="cap">capitalize: the quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
